# Build-context excludes for the gateway image.
#
# Root cause this fixes: with no .dockerignore, `COPY app/ app/` (and the other
# COPYs) baked in every __pycache__ dir — so deleted packages survived in the
# image as empty PEP-420 namespace dirs (stale *.pyc), and the build context
# shipped the entire multi-GB workspace/ to the daemon on every build.
#
# Safe by construction: the Dockerfile COPYs only specific paths
# (requirements.txt, app/, wiki/, raw/, wiki_schema/, dashboard/{public,build},
# scripts/, tests/, entrypoint.sh). Nothing below is among them — `git` is
# apt-installed and shinka-evolve is pulled from a remote URL, so the local
# .git is unused at build; workspace/ is only `mkdir`'d in-image then
# bind-mounted at runtime.

# Python bytecode / packaging / tool caches
**/__pycache__/
**/*.py[cod]
**/*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/
**/.mypy_cache/
**/.ruff_cache/

# VCS
.git/
.gitignore

# Runtime data — never COPY'd (bind-mounted at runtime)
workspace/

# JS deps + local dev cruft (dashboard/build is COPY'd; the React source tree is not)
node_modules/
dashboard-react/node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
*.log
.DS_Store
